  "command": "bash research_loop/results/MECH-KEYS/launch_mech_keys.sh",
  "observations": "PART A. `rewrite_keys_on_support` gained an opt-in `reposition` flag (`AM_KEY_REPOSITION` -> `AttentionMatchingFinetuningConfig.key_reposition`, default off) that counter-rotates every DOCUMENT-sourced key by `-doc_rope_offset` through `phase1._rope_reposition` at the configured `rope_theta`; cartridge-sourced rows are left untouched. Unit check on CUDA at T_doc=4000, theta=5e6, 16 doc-sourced installs: the gap between the logit the installed key delivers in the student frame and the logit the selector actually used falls from max 1.0540 / mean 0.2358 to max 4.77e-07 / mean 4.99e-08 in float32 and to max 5.52e-03 / mean 6.23e-04 in the cache's bf16, on a score scale of max|s| = 2.779; cartridge-sourced rows are exactly 0.0 in both arms. At the primitive level over this project's real document lengths (T_doc = 3858 / 4000 / 8900) the relative error drops 1.041 / 0.945 / 1.203 -> 1.98e-07 / 2.03e-07 / 2.15e-07 and the correlation with the intended logit rises 0.510 / 0.430 / 0.327 -> 1.000. Doing the same counter-rotation at the AM package's historical theta=1e4 gives max errors 4.43 / 5.02 / 5.11 -- larger than not correcting at all, so the true base is load-bearing. Bit-identical when off: `rewrite_keys_on_support` at default arguments matches `git show HEAD:` to max|delta| = 0.0 for both `highest_attention` and `omp`; the freeze end-to-end write matches a `git archive HEAD` snapshot run in a separate interpreter on mean_mse, per-layer MSE, key/value sums, |v|max, mass_on_S and the `extra` key set. PART B. The control (KEY_MODE=freeze) reproduced DIAG-ROPE arm B to all 17 printed digits in-run (QA 2.15320086479187 / MT 2.5296061038970947), with mean `am/mean_mse` 0.014059890443260059 and |v|max 178.0 identical to MECH-BETA's rope arm, and its standalone evals (QA 2.159724712371826 / MT 2.529625177383423) match that run's standalone numbers exactly. The pre-loop folklore that key rewriting collapses QA is FALSE in this setting: every key arm improved BOTH axes. keys+reposition gave QA 2.03492 / MT 2.33050 standalone (in-run 2.03495 / 2.32901), i.e. dQA -0.125 and dMT -0.199 against the control; keys without reposition gave QA 2.12011 / MT 2.42385 (dMT -0.106); OMP+reposition gave QA 2.11686 / MT 2.39698 (dMT -0.133). The H2 fix is worth a further -0.093 MT and -0.085 QA on top of the uncorrected key write. MT 2.3305 is below ORACLE-WRITE's perfect-value-write ceiling (2.381) and below the k=12 snapshot minimum (2.435); it is still 0.31 above the win bar (2.02). The selectivity metric barely moved: eval-time MT/QA mass_on_S ratio is 1.0428 (control), 1.0485 (keys, no reposition), 1.0510 (keys+reposition), 1.0638 (OMP) -- versus the untouched Phase-1 cartridge's own 1.0812. keys+reposition bought +0.0082 of ratio, the same order as beta's +0.008, yet unlike beta it improved CE on both axes. What did move is raw bandwidth: eval-time mass_on_S on MT rose 0.0711 -> 0.3756 (no reposition) / 0.2430 (reposition) / 0.1918 (OMP), and total cartridge mass 0.593 -> 0.720 / 0.671 / 0.645. Part of the reposition/OMP bandwidth is a support-size effect -- their written union widens to 87.6 and 105.2 slots/layer against the control's 53.4 -- but the no-reposition arm sits at 51.6 slots/layer, SMALLER than the control, and still carries 5.3x the mass, so the bandwidth gain is not merely a wider support. Keys actually rewritten: of the 32 support slots per (layer, head, document), a document key won 8.91 on average without reposition (27.8% of 147,456 slot-writes), 12.91 with reposition (40.3%) and 17.86 under OMP (55.8%); 29.5-30.7 of 32 support slots changed key vector in every case. `n_repositioned_total` equals `n_from_doc_total` exactly in both reposition arms (59,478 and 82,318), and the last document's rope_delta was -6335 (= its T_doc). Document 1 installs the same 5,309 doc keys in both highest_attention arms -- the counter-rotation changes the installed vector, not the selection -- and they diverge from document 2 onward. The solve's own metric improved with keys too (mean `am/mean_mse` 0.014060 -> 0.003844 / 0.003941 / 0.004843) and the write got gentler (|v|max 178 -> 63.25 / 74.0 / 141.0). Cost: solve_s 182 s (control) -> 325 s / 272 s, but OMP is 3857 s (21x the control) for a worse result than highest_attention+reposition; gradient_steps = 0 everywhere. B-OVERWRITE interaction: the per-document `cache-after-doc-*.pt` snapshots were saved for all four arms but were NOT evaluated (see `skipped`); the per-document install counts are reported instead, and they are far flatter across documents with the fix (3308-5309, ratio 1.6) than without it (1880-5309, ratio 2.8). Caveats: MT n=69 / QA n=78, so dMT -0.199 sits at the top edge of the 0.1-0.2 noise band and dQA -0.125 sits inside it; one seed; no seed variation was run; and all four arms were SIGKILLed at CUDA teardown after their artifacts and wandb sync completed (see `exit_codes_note`).",
